  "intendedUsers": [
    "Local reviewers of care processes"
  ],
  "interpretation": {
    "meaning": "The signed time in minutes from the recorded HbA1c collection time to the recorded creatinine collection time (positive when creatinine was collected later), and which was collected first. A missing time is never treated as zero. Version 0.1.1 also says whether the two recorded collection times fall within a window a local clinician supplies; with no window supplied that output reads parameter-not-enabled. Version 0.1.2 also counts how many of four listed facts are recorded; it is a count of recorded facts, not a measure of care.",
    "prohibited": [
      "Do not read the gap as a statement about the quality or timeliness of care.",
      "Do not use any output as a recommendation, alert or order.",
      "A window is a description of the record, not a standard of care."
    ]
  },
  "limitations": {
    "items": [
      "A missing diabetes collection time gives needs-data; a missing kidney collection time gives indeterminate, because the kidney context is optional in the group and its absence must never read as normal.",
      "It reads the recorded collection times only; no evaluation time is used.",
      "No window and no edge rule are supplied: both parameters are disabled, so the window output reads parameter-not-enabled until a named local clinician enables them.",
      "Nothing reads as complete: the count has no expected number. A missing kidney context gives indeterminate, not a low count.",
      "The two conversion factors are unit definitions with no reviewed source. A converted value is shown, never judged, and no threshold exists."
    ],
    "statement": "Describes when samples were recorded as collected. It says nothing about any value, about the quality or timeliness of care, or about a trend, and it is not decision support."
  },
